                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game unclogged my pores. \r\nUknon Jones is one of the most stable, usable video games of the 20th century. A true sequel to Sonichu in every way.\r\n\r\nThe keyboard controls are unique, but clearly serve a purpose. The game is (I believe) split between three main characters - Uknon, Guynelk, and Lisa, played here by white Nicki Minaj. This is reflected in how you have to split your arms between three locations on the keyboard and mouse at any given time.\r\n\r\nExpedition 33, also made by baguette munching, cheese sniffing Frenchman, clearly took heavy inspiration from this epic rendition of Homer's Ilyiad. \r\n\r\nUnfortunately, the game crashed every time I tried to enter the first level, but I believe that that was actually a metaphor, a similie if you will, about modern gaming and how they often push out games unfinished. This avant garde approach to game design meant I got to experience the majority of what the game had to offer in just 17 minutes.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1755666946,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1755666946,
                        "voted_up": true,
                        "votes_up": 4,
                        "votes_funny": 12,
                        "weighted_vote_score": 0.5857474207878113,
